                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "For equal initial investments, compare the growth factors over the full terms.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For the same initial investment $P$:\n$$\\begin{align*}I_A&=P(1.065)^6-P\\\\I_A&=P\\bigl((1.065)^6-1\\bigr)\\\\I_A&\\approx0.4591423P\\\\I_B&=P(1.053)^8-P\\\\I_B&=P\\bigl((1.053)^8-1\\bigr)\\\\I_B&\\approx0.5115655P\\end{align*}$$\nBank B yields the greater interest over its full investment term.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If a customer invests $\\$10\\,000$ in Bank A, how much would she have to invest with Bank B to produce the same amount produced by Bank A at the end of the investment period? Give your answer to the nearest cent.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$9653.19$",
          "worked": "Let $P_B$ be the initial investment in Bank B. Equate the amounts at the ends of the respective investment terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}P_B(1.053)^8&=10\\,000(1.065)^6\\\\P_B&=\\frac{10\\,000(1.065)^6}{(1.053)^8}\\\\P_B&\\approx\\$9653.19\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
